{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e","id":839512,"title":"Other shapeshifters and skinchangers in 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-29T16:26:40-08:00","id":839512,"title":"Other shapeshifters and skinchangers in 2e?","content":"Is there any hinting that they're still part of the setting or will be included in any future supplements? How much of Skinchangers still works, and how much needs tweaking for the 2e rules?<br /> <br /> If there's no chance of anything official showing up, any interest in homebrewing some types of alternate shifters for 2e? The lack of them is literally my least favorite thing about the setting, which has plenty of interesting aspects that I feel are kind of wasted by limiting the players to just being wolves. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'm really hoping OP takes another shot at other shapeshifters in a future book. 2e is a perfect chance to make up for The Book That Must Not Be Named.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T16:40:05-08:00","id":839525,"title":"","content":"Odds are it will come up in a later book.<br /> <br /> We've had many threads on the subject, I believe I'm the main proponent of getting away from a were-zoo. There are more than a few homebrewed shapeshifters in the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T17:02:17-08:00","id":839543,"title":"","content":"Skinchangers now are basically Wolf-Blooded with &quot;Skinner&quot; Tell and if you wish, you can adapt it more akin to Skin Thief facet of Gift of Change (Wolf Gift). Another alternative is to construct Horror using 2ed CofD rules with Dread Powers like Skin-Taker (this time from Werewolf 2ed). If you want more, then you can model it a bit like werewolf forms or even better - like Idigam. You know, creature having &quot;true form&quot; that is stronger, but also have some unique Bane and Bane. I also think on this forum there were some homebrews about shapechangers under Helios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7871-miriander","name":"Miriander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:49:29-08:00","id":840477,"title":"","content":"I'd be the first to jump at such a project. Seriously, it's on my character sheet and everything! &quot;<b>Changing Breeds: </b>Claire gains an infinite bonus to her Initiative when acting to be part of any new Changing Breeds book.&quot; The Fera were my favorite things in the oWoD and also include my favorite playable species in a game (the Mokol\u00e9), and I would enjoy having the opportunity to bring more werebeasts and skin-changers into the Chronicles. Note that, like every book is assumed to be, this is part of a toolkit experience, so you wouldn't have to include all or even any of them in your games. No werezoo unless you want to include everything, but for those who do want some variety, you can have your werecrocodiles and weresharks and wereparaceratheriums. The last one might be a joke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Maybe.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:52:56-08:00","id":840478,"title":"","content":"Werefoxes without creepy baggage or a balance so bad it makes my brain want to eat someone elses liver?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'd write that in a heartbeat too. Changing Breed 2: Shift Happens, let's pitch it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T01:20:30-08:00","id":840485,"title":"","content":"A toolbox (even by WoD standards) for new shifters could be a ton of fun. The sort of toolbox that gives you the options you need to create entire gameline protagonists like &quot;wolf shifters that police the borders of the spirit world&quot; or &quot;spider shifter's who's webs let only the virtuous dead onwards in the afterlife&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T01:29:14-08:00","id":840487,"title":"","content":"So long as each shifter has thematic depth beyond &quot;like the werewolves, but a different animal instead!&quot; I'll be happy. <br /> <br /> Doubly so if we get servants of Helios, either expanded Baal-Hadad or something weirder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T02:38:46-08:00","id":840500,"title":"","content":"Beyond the basic affinity of being shape-shifters I've always wondered what the point of the changing breeds are. Do they all serve some special purpose like the Uratha, or are they around just cause?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:02:07-08:00","id":840541,"title":"","content":"Clearly, a were-deer's maximum can't be that it must hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:40:28-08:00","id":840552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840541#post840541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, a were-deer's maximum can't be that it must hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because the maxim of actual deer and most wild animals is must hunt. The world revolves around its stomach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:41:56-08:00","id":840554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840500#post840500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the basic affinity of being shape-shifters I've always wondered what the point of the changing breeds are. Do they all serve some special purpose like the Uratha, or are they around just cause?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that they had their own&quot;Father Wolfs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:49:22-08:00","id":840558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840552#post840552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Because the maxim of actual deer and most wild animals is must hunt. The world revolves around its stomach.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather stretching the word 'hunt' in the case of herbivores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:56:23-08:00","id":840562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e#post839512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any hinting that they're still part of the setting or will be included in any future supplements? How much of Skinchangers still works, and how much needs tweaking for the 2e rules?<br /> <br /> If there's no chance of anything official showing up, any interest in homebrewing some types of alternate shifters for 2e? The lack of them is literally my least favorite thing about the setting, which has plenty of interesting aspects that I feel are kind of wasted by limiting the players to just being wolves.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm really hoping OP takes another shot at other shapeshifters in a future book. 2e is a perfect chance to make up for The Book That Must Not Be Named.</div> </div> </div> </div>All three types of &quot;fera&quot; in the Chronicles of Darkness (Skinchangers, War Against the Pure, and Changing Breeds) have mentions in upcoming books I'm aware of. The Neolithic setting in Dark Eras has the WATP Helios-worshipping minotaur shifters in it, the Aztec setting has Skinchanger Jaguar warriors, and my story in the Beast Fiction Anthology has a Bastet in it.<br /> <br /> They didn't drop out of the setting in the ongoing edition change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:26:34-08:00","id":840575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840541#post840541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, a were-deer's maximum can't be that it must hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deer/Gazelle/Elk/Antelope/Cow/Sheep/Giraffe/Goat/Muskox/Buffalo Must Graze.<br /> <br /> Seriously with the advent of Pangaeans you have access to elements, plants, trees, weapons, cities, emotions, dreams, stellar phenomena, even ideologies and weather patterns. Why do people always just want 'werewolves but with another animal?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-02-2016, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:53:09-08:00","id":840580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840575#post840575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deer/Gazelle/Elk/Antelope/Cow/Sheep/Giraffe/Goat/Muskox/Buffalo Must Graze.<br /> <br /> Seriously with the advent of Pangaeans you have access to elements, plants, trees, weapons, cities, emotions, dreams, stellar phenomena, even ideologies and weather patterns. Why do people always just want 'werewolves but with another animal?'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it's easier to empathize and understand werrebeasts as opposed to wereweapons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also there's the fact that shapeshifting is a cool and wondrous thing and other nonabimals will not have that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:00:25-08:00","id":840582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840580#post840580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's easier to empathize and understand werrebeasts as opposed to wereweapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like a spirit of the hunt? Werewolves aren't animals, they're hunters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also there's the fact that shapeshifting is a cool and wondrous thing and other nonabimals will not have that </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's true, no one in the history of fiction has ever turned into fire or other elements, or transformed into an anthropomorphic representative of other concepts, like Sandman's Endless. And there are a lot of movies about weregazelle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:09:26-08:00","id":840590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840575#post840575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deer/Gazelle/Elk/Antelope/Cow/Sheep/Giraffe/Goat/Muskox/Buffalo Must Graze.<br /> <br /> Seriously with the advent of Pangaeans you have access to elements, plants, trees, weapons, cities, emotions, dreams, stellar phenomena, even ideologies and weather patterns. Why do people always just want 'werewolves but with another animal?'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're thinking of Changeling.<br /> <br /> Edit: Which isn't to say your musing isn't wrong, but the sort of game that has what you're thinking of is Changeling, with all the strangeness of being that falling star and yet you're undoubtedly human as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:14:15-08:00","id":840593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840590#post840590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of Changeling.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Which isn't to say your musing isn't wrong, but the sort of game that has what you're thinking of is Changeling, with all the strangeness of being that falling star and yet you're undoubtedly human as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm thinking of Werewolf the Forsaken. Thus the riff off the Werewolf the Forsaken catch phrase, and taking spirit choirs directly from the Werewolf the Forsaken Predators book.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are spirit-flesh hybrids of the hunt. There are spirits for everything that exists in the world, except humans. There is no reason to limit Changing Breeds to animals, because spirits are not limited to animals and, frankly, animals aren't even remotely a subject of the game, they're just the lens it's shown through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:24:37-08:00","id":840598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840558#post840558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's rather stretching the word 'hunt' in the case of herbivores.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forage, hunt, it's a matter of semantics. At least most predators kill their prey before before consuming. Plants get eaten alive. And don't get me started on chewing. What a violent, violent business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:28:54-08:00","id":840601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840575#post840575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deer/Gazelle/Elk/Antelope/Cow/Sheep/Giraffe/Goat/Muskox/Buffalo Must Graze.<br /> <br /> Seriously with the advent of Pangaeans you have access to elements, plants, trees, weapons, cities, emotions, dreams, stellar phenomena, even ideologies and weather patterns. Why do people always just want 'werewolves but with another animal?'</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that simple. IMO, different species owe fealty to different parent spirits and serve different purposes. A weredeer's maxim might be 'must protect'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:35:02-08:00","id":840606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840593#post840593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are spirit-flesh hybrids of the hunt. There are spirits for everything that exists in the world, except humans. There is no reason to limit Changing Breeds to animals, because spirits are not limited to animals and, frankly, animals aren't even remotely a subject of the game, they're just the lens it's shown through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from but I think this would be very challenging and to some extent, Claimed are already designed to fulfill this role. Animal-human hybrids tend to work best because, as animals themselves, humans have the easiest time identifying with other animals.<br /> <br /> What would it even mean to be a weremountain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:52:21-08:00","id":840613,"title":"","content":"I suppose writing things half asleep while in a car tends to create quick replies without elaboration on my end. I'll address what I mean.<br /> <br /> I meant that it's <i>easier </i>to write a game involving werecreatures as opposed to nontraditional entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840582#post840582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like a spirit of the hunt? Werewolves aren't animals, they're hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but werewolves also tie that in with wolves, it's kind of self explanatory really in their title.<br /> If you want to do a different concept without relating to another animal <i>at all</i>, you need to do more work. Not just in mechanics and crunch, but also in writing. Animals come prepackaged with loads of concepts that they relate to that you can draw from and select.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I suppose that's true, no one in the history of fiction has ever turned into fire or other elements, or transformed into an anthropomorphic representative of other concepts, like Sandman's Endless. And there are a lot of movies about weregazelle. </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifting would be harder to write as well.<br /> It'd would be possible here, but any writer would need to go through more creative hoops. This is especially true when you attach that restriction of &quot;no animals&quot;. There's work arounds like angelic beings and other supernatural stuff like living shadows and bones, and whatever... but such fantastic forms are not always suited towards the camoflague role.<br /> <br /> You'd also need to expend more creative thought to designing the forms, more if you do try to expand on it to equal the five forms of the animal/human scale.<br /> It would be easy sure to create the human, near human, and half-human-and-other forms. Self explanatory. The others would be dicier.<br /> <br /> I mean for instance. Let's take an earth elemental from say a mountain god.<br /> <br /> He's got: <br /> Man form<br /> Tougher human form.<br /> A form like a stone golem.<br /> <br /> So is he supposed to turn into a boulder for his other forms. I guess it's camo, but well, is he supposed to remain in animate?<br /> The same goes for &quot;weretree&quot;<br /> This gets even more confusing when you want to do &quot;Werecities&quot;; does an entire city block spawn from no where? What about were-emotions?<br /> I mean, how does your completely non-human form work without doing animals peroid?<br /> <br /> <br /> To make a long story short, I take the view that it's easier to write about werecreatures than other things. Perhaps you can call it laziness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:07:38-08:00","id":840622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840601#post840601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that simple. IMO, different species owe fealty to different parent spirits and serve different purposes. A weredeer's maxim might be 'must protect'.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing is not a spirit of deer, it's a spirit of protection. It could be a shield, a fire, a mountain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840606#post840606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see where you're coming from but I think this would be very challenging and to some extent, Claimed are already designed to fulfill this role.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really don't, at all. Claimed are spirits possessing objects, animals and people in the real world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Animal-human hybrids tend to work best because, as animals themselves, humans have the easiest time identifying with other animals. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean they work best, just as Almarck says, it's the laziest way to go about it.<br /> <br /> I'll certainly agree that some were-animals make sense, Claire Redfield's done an admirable job with it, but there's no reason to <i>only </i>have a were-animal menagerie and never think beyond it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would it even mean to be a weremountain? </div> </div> </div>What do mountains symbolize? Permanence, immovability, fortitde, obstacles on paths to greater things or danger. From there you have long-lived and hearty beings that challenge others to better themselves or treacherously to doom them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840613#post840613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animals come prepackaged with loads of concepts that they relate to that you can draw from and select.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thousands of years of civilization have given you the same amounts of concepts regarding almost every other thing that exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shapeshifting would be harder to write as well.<br /> ...but such fantastic forms are not always suited towards the camoflague role... more if you do try to expand on it to equal the five forms of the animal/human scale. </div> </div> </div>It really wouldn't. Werewolves camouflauge themselves because, as hunters, if they do not, their prey will escape. It's part of the hunt. Not everything needs to be the same. Just like the five forms, each one helps them in one aspect of the hunt. There's no reason for everything else to have five forms as well. A Mountain Man could be an individual with the Giant merit. Maybe they can turn to stone when being assailed, or merge into mountains. They don't need to actually have a man, near-man, mountain-man, near-mountain, mountain form, any more than a deer does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This gets even more confusing when you want to do &quot;Werecities&quot;; does an entire city block spawn from no where? What about were-emotions? </div> </div> </div>No, you have something like John Hawksmoor from the Authority. A Man of Cities. Were-emotions would resemble some of the thousands of examples we've had of rageful beings throughout history. Something demonic, red-skinned, heated and steaming or smoking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:09:15-08:00","id":840624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840575#post840575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deer/Gazelle/Elk/Antelope/Cow/Sheep/Giraffe/Goat/Muskox/Buffalo Must Graze.<br /> <br /> Seriously with the advent of Pangaeans you have access to elements, plants, trees, weapons, cities, emotions, dreams, stellar phenomena, even ideologies and weather patterns. Why do people always just want 'werewolves but with another animal?'</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. You may have quoted the wrong person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:11:14-08:00","id":840625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840624#post840624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. You may have quoted the wrong person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was just adding to your comment, then wondering 'aloud.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:14:29-08:00","id":840628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840562#post840562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Neolithic setting in Dark Eras has the WATP Helios-worshipping minotaur shifters in it,</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh cool, I can mention that now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, I know how I'd do a new version of Changing Breeds. It'd look quite a lot different to the 1e version, for sure. Among other things it'd be more horror-focused.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers is a bit of a different creature; part of it has been eaten by the new Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:01:01-08:00","id":840660,"title":"","content":"For a while I've felt that the essential problem* of Changing Breeds was trying to be cWoD in nWoD, and it just didn't fit or work at all as that. But I like the concept of additional shifters in the CofD/nWoD, and it has a lot of material worth exploring. The shifters in WATP for instance, were quite unique and very thematically different from the Uratha. They're a good example of what I'd want to see in a Forsaken 2e supplement about other shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Aside from the questionable writing, abysmal mechanical balance and groan-inducing baggage, which I feel stemmed at least in part from the mistaken premise.</span><br /> <br /> So yeah, would welcome a project like that. I have full confidence in the Werewolf team to do the subject justice if they tackle it. It's practically dripping with fuel for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-02-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:53:09-08:00","id":840691,"title":"","content":"Fine, I'll concede, on the &quot;why-no-werecars&quot; (good Futurama ep btw) matter nofather. I am still not convinced that it would work out even if technically plausible.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking on your original statement, I think the answer is probably more that of people who are into Werewolf are interested in playing &quot;werecreatures&quot;, but are not willing to make the jump into more esoteric spirit hybrids. Because while technically plausible, it is a hard sell due to the very wide gap between &quot;creatures&quot; to &quot;things&quot;. Not on a conceptual level, but rather a... comfort level perhaps. Other werecreatures existing aren't as taxing or requiring as much work.<br /> <br /> Granted, Changeling is able to handle the issue, but that gameline has different setting assumptions as well as a different audience even though there is overlap. There's also the fact that, well, all of the various forms you can take are given very basic representation at the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 03-02-2016, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:07:20-08:00","id":840700,"title":"","content":"Other shapeshifters = Azlu and Beshilu. Spider and rat shifters are in the core book. I would dearly love to see more Hosts all around; they've always been my favorite prey, and they fill the whole other-half-spirit-shapeshifter theme in a way that's intimately tied into the game and immediately relevant. <br /> <br /> Playable non-wolf shifterhood is currently not a thing. How much of 1e stuff is still viable? Well, fluffwise, all of it. Mechanically, none of it. You'll need to translate pretty much everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:52:18-08:00","id":840731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840622#post840622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing is not a spirit of deer, it's a spirit of protection. It could be a shield, a fire, a mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same line of thinking why would we have werewolves? They're spirits of the hunt not the spirits of wolves. The could just as easily be a gun, a fire, an avalanche.<br /> <br /> So, not seeing it. Also not seeing the mechanics. The primal form of a mountain is...a mountain. Now what? Your character as no animus in that form.<br /> <br /> At best these things would be W:tF versions of Changeling seemings. The question is, does W:tF really need such a thing? Once you introduce such things what is the impact going to be on game play? <br /> <br /> I don't think the whole &quot;zoo menagerie&quot; thing is lazy, or a problem. Asking and answering the question of where a weredeer fits into the existing W:tF setting (both mechanically and fluff-wise) is much easier than answering the same question for weremountains. (And really, I think that part of the problem may be that folks have a tendency to overthink the setting fluff. Werewolves explanation for their existence may be that they are spirits of the hunt but in reality they might simply be lycanthropes -- half-human / half-animal. There are no HARD TRUTHS in Chronicles of Darkness games.)<br /> <br /> YMMV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:56:52-08:00","id":840734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840622#post840622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thousands of years of civilization have given you the same amounts of concepts regarding almost every other thing that exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>So werenumbers? Yes, I think I'll play a were-5.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the snark, but I feel like we slipped off a slope somewhere a while back. We limit it to animals because we need to draw a hard line somewhere and we already have one kind of animal -- wolves -- so why not just stick to animals? If we extend to inanimate objects it's only a matter of time until we inevitably get to weremoney (because its an inanimate object too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:20:46-08:00","id":840754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840731#post840731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same line of thinking why would we have werewolves? They're spirits of the hunt not the spirits of wolves. The could just as easily be a gun, a fire, an avalanche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because from the period in history they spawn from wolves were the most representative of the hunt, but also to fit into the original Universal Monsters concept. I believe that, in world, if werewolves were to be created now we would have werecats or wereguns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, not seeing it. Also not seeing the mechanics. The primal form of a mountain is...a mountain. Now what? Your character as no animus in that form. </div> </div> </div>I said before I was against just copying the original five form aspects for everything else, but if you chose to go with a mountain form you could have something similar to a Beast's Lair. A mountainous pass full of obstacles to protect the mountain's heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At best these things would be W:tF versions of Changeling seemings. The question is, does W:tF really need such a thing? Once you introduce such things what is the impact going to be on game play? </div> </div> </div>It needs them as much as it needs other Changing Breeds. But they're no more or less versions of Changeling seemings than werewolves themselves are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the whole &quot;zoo menagerie&quot; thing is lazy, or a problem. Asking and answering the question of where a weredeer fits into the existing W:tF setting (both mechanically and fluff-wise) is much easier than answering the same question for weremountains. (And really, I think that part of the problem may be that folks have a tendency to overthink the setting fluff. </div> </div> </div>You yourself said they would hunt. How does that fit into a game of Werewolf?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves explanation for their existence may be that they are spirits of the hunt but in reality they might simply be lycanthropes -- half-human / half-animal. There are no HARD TRUTHS in Chronicles of Darkness games.)YMMV </div> </div> </div>There's many hard truths in Chronicles of Darkness games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So werenumbers? Yes, I think I'll play a were-5.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the snark,</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> No need to apologize, I have the same eye rolling when people want to have were-animals for every kind of animal. I see no point. What is a wereantelope bringing to the table that a weregazelle isn't, that also isn't covered by a weredeer? Why are any of them necessary, or even wanted? It seems to be the kneejerk insistence of some that if there are werewolves, there must be were-every other animal, but why? I could understand if it was just 'I want to play a deer,' but no one has said that, they just want weredeer to exist for some reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We limit it to animals because we need to draw a hard line somewhere and we already have one kind of animal -- wolves -- so why not just stick to animals? If we extend to inanimate objects it's only a matter of time until we inevitably get to weremoney (because its an inanimate object too). </div> </div> </div>Dollars and coins are objects, money is a concept, but you already have examples of this in fiction with representations of greed. Still, nowhere did I say every place, thing or idea should have a were-variant, but the idea that there needs to be a hard line somewhere and you need to draw it is silly.<br /> <br /> YMMV.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:27:27-08:00","id":840759,"title":"","content":"Don't forget emotions and concepts. Were-schadenfruede, Were-music, etc.<br /> <br /> But joking aside, what other concepts make sense? Father Wolf was a spirit (or Pangaean) of the Hunt, who also happened to identify as a wolf. Had kids with a Celestine, which survive to this day. A similar concept would need to jump through similar hoops. Hosts are similar, but different. Most spiritual representations would be Claimed. You might do a few lineages of Claimed, but they wouldn't have the varied hooks and drives of the Uratha. Urfarah provides the wolf link and the Hunt aspects. Luna allows for the shifting. History accounts for their silver bane, Tribes, duty, etc.<br /> <br /> Anything remotely equivalent will need a fair amount of backstory to be anything other than a one-off worth little note.<br /> <br /> Though I do remember some not-quite Raven-host in one book? <hr /><br /> And because criticism without alternative ideas rubs some people the wrong way:<br /> <br /> <i>A long time ago, there was the [Pact/Pantheon/Guardians/Whatever], a small choir/group of spirits that wanted to see and enjoy the world of flesh. Or something. At first conflicting with Urfarah, they eventually struck a deal to abide by certain rules when travelling beyond the Border Marches</i><i> (alternatively, they tricked the great hunter and snuck past). Keeping their influence small, they found compatible humans to &quot;ride&quot; with, each member taking a turn to enjoy the world with the human, and offering the human power in return. After the Gauntlet arose and cut them off from their homes in the Shadow, the [Whatever] developed a plan for their survival - they would merge with their human allies, with each human containing a fragment from one of the [Whatever], which they would pass on to their progeny, when circumstances were auspicious. These bloodlines have continued down to today, with members occasionally awakening the dormant shards of the [Whatever] inside them.</i><br /> <br /> Maps to Werewolves with:<br /> Alternate forms -&gt; whichever spirit-member is riding shotgun at the time<br /> Potential powers -&gt; reclaimed spirit Numina, Gifts just like Uratha, or Dread Powers like Claimed (which they closely resemble)<br /> History allows for their existence.<br /> Need for subtly (through stealth or pact) explains why they aren't common and can be dropped in without prior notice.<br /> They do need some other reason for existence, though. Maybe to &quot;experience the world&quot;? Bon Vivant to the Werewolf's Hunter? Or maintain the &quot;Sacred Places&quot; (Loci)? Or Teach Humanity (a mirror of Beast's justification)?<br /> <br /> Whatever, I came up with it in a few minutes. Can easily state the spirit members where a group of animals, or related concepts, with one being the animal of choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-02-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:40:43-08:00","id":840764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840487#post840487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So long as each shifter has thematic depth beyond &quot;like the werewolves, but a different animal instead!&quot; I'll be happy.<br /> <br /> Doubly so if we get servants of Helios, either expanded Baal-Hadad or something weirder.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had anything to with a second batch of werecreatures book, rest assured the idea would be to deliver nothing but <i>weirdness</i>. Playable, awesome weirdness.<br /> <br /> THough Dave brings up a valid point about all of the old stuff being valid-though in my mind, that reads as an invite to go, clean up, and make awesome.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For clarity, I would aim more blue book than Werewolf. I'd want to divorce a great number of the shifters away from the Flesh/Shadow dichotomy, and even from a majority of the other gamelines, and get weird with different lineages.<br /> <br /> One of the neat things about doing it that way is that we could revisit some werecreatures that might have been given a rough treatment *coughchangingbreedscough* and create a new spin that doesn't invalidate older versions for them.<br /> <br /> Also, expecting different cosmological backgrounds would give me a way to break the cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-02-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:06:36-08:00","id":840785,"title":"","content":"But Arc, would you bring back the all-important sidebar about furries being more likely to become one of the Changing Breeds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:53:34-08:00","id":840811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840785#post840785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Arc, would you bring back the all-important sidebar about furries being more likely to become one of the Changing Breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't forget the sidebar about the complications of having sex with your dog!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:00:19-08:00","id":840814,"title":"","content":"I <i>liked</i> in <b>Changing Breed</b> that Breeds itself had their own, unique backgrounds - but also not as weird as some stuff in <b>WAtP</b>. Maybe totally unified mythology of &quot;Nature&quot; was a bad way to doing in <b>CB</b>, but making werecats as obsessed hive mind made me cringe in <b>WAtP</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I will surely cheer developers of new <b>Changing Breeds</b> 2ED ( or whatever it will be called ), but it will be a tough nut to crack - to make various, more horror oriented backgrounds and somehow coherent.<br /> <br /> If my add - I would <i>love</i> to see Bastets made like <b>Sleepwalkers</b>from movie ( or really Bubasti from <b>CB</b> )- maybe it was not best picture in the world, but those monsters were <i>really</i> scary, in totally different way that werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7MDUbjbTZos\" data-code=\"7MDUbjbTZos\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7MDUbjbTZos/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Also, my avatar is so much demanding scary/lovable werebears. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:00:56-08:00","id":840815,"title":"","content":"Honestly I would like it if at least some of the shifters had access to gifts. But yeah I like the different weirdness. Keeping skin thieves is okay as long as they clean up the mechanics. I want them to have major template power hence I like gifts rather then a few crappy mutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:01:47-08:00","id":840816,"title":"","content":"See, I'm not with you there wyrd. War Against the Pure was my ideal level of weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:04:52-08:00","id":840818,"title":"","content":"Nah. I'd just hired the guy who does the sex dog memes* and have him put in a picture anywhere said sidebars should be.[/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> But yeah, the sex disclaimer would be a big, bold, thing on the opposite side of the table of contents, saying simple &quot;DON'T HAVE SEX WITH ANIMALS.&quot; with an implied dickhead in there.<br /> <br /> As for furries, none of them, except <i>that one</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Rooster Teeth Short, that's what I'm referencing. I am not talking beastiality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:11:01-08:00","id":840823,"title":"","content":"Furry gameline confirmed for after Deviant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:15:27-08:00","id":840827,"title":"","content":"Furry Chapter, maybe. Be cool to have a lycanthropic &quot;be careful what you wish for&quot; sort of thing, after growing up in my youth wanting to be a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:24:14-08:00","id":840837,"title":"","content":".... avoiding a..... repugnant topic, my big concern with &quot;different flavors of weirdness&quot; is going to be the mechanical handling of it.<br /> <br /> And obviously not all shape changers would be as magical as others.<br /> <br /> How I see it is first dividing lesser shape changers from greater shape changers.<br /> <br /> Lesser shape changers is a mini template, like ghoul or wolfbloodism. Think old skintheives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Greater would be.... well the full thing. Power stats, different forms, origin stories, ect.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think like the old book we would have some central mechanics like Primal urge, but unlike the old book, I think each shape changer splat would have more unique mechanics pertaining to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance in my current veiw, all shape changers have a Primal urge and Harmony.<br /> <br /> But the effects and specific rules of primal urge vary, not all of them regenerate, some have gifts, others have numina. Others use nanomachines. The specifics of these are listed in a shape changer races entry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:39:43-08:00","id":840845,"title":"","content":"I am curious what the repugnant topic is.<br /> <br /> Mechanical handling would definitely be a thing to pay attention too, particularly since I would want to do a variety of template experiments, from merit based templates to mini-greater templates ala Purified. But a lot of how deviant it all gets comes from how the pitch works out.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, fuck it, I guess I'm gonna work out a pitch with other interested parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:43:01-08:00","id":840848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840660#post840660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Aside from the questionable writing, abysmal mechanical balance and groan-inducing baggage, which I feel stemmed at least in part from the mistaken premise.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://destroythis.blogspot.com/search?updated-max=2014-07-31T18:46:00-07:00&amp;max-results=7&amp;start=7&amp;by-date=false&amp;m=1\" target=\"_blank\">A review, point by point, of all this baggage.</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:04:44-08:00","id":840870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840845#post840845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious what the repugnant topic is.<br /> <br /> Mechanical handling would definitely be a thing to pay attention too, particularly since I would want to do a variety of template experiments, from merit based templates to mini-greater templates ala Purified. But a lot of how deviant it all gets comes from how the pitch works out.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, fuck it, I guess I'm gonna work out a pitch with other interested parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd offer to help, but I am not a free lancer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:22:07-08:00","id":840880,"title":"","content":"Wow, I am psyched that there seems to be this much interested in this. <br /> <br /> I have kind of wondered what it would be like to completely do away with werewolves and run a Spirit-focused game based more on Persona, where the players were humans who had bonded with spirits of various types. I've always loved the idea of the Shadow and found it a bit unfortunate that it was so limited to werewolves (I've never really been a wolfaboo), BUT at this point that wouldn't really work, since it would probably end up just being Geist With Spirits. It'd be cool to have some more support for mortal spiritualists and Claimed, though...<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the zoo! I actually like keeping shifters connected to the Shadow, and having them all fundamentally be some sort of human-spirit combination. Because, as I said before, the Shadow is a huge, HUGE setting with almost infinite possibility, and the more ways of exploring that, the better. <br /> <br /> If we do get more Helios-servants, I really hope they're some variety of werereptiles. I mean, it works thematically, since reptiles=sun. Although, honestly, I mostly just want it because I LOVE reptiles. Maybe even make them more technologically/civilization-focused than Werewolves? It makes for a good dichotomy, and there's a lot of mythological association between reptiles and knowledge/cunning/so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:24:37-08:00","id":840882,"title":"","content":"If Helios Servants are to be done, I want more on the Baal-Hadaad.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we have the War of the Pure and even a good amount of Skinchangers focused on the Shadow. Again, as far as my own interests goes, that's a cue to me to say &quot;Time to break the mold.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:27:23-08:00","id":840883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840882#post840882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Helios Servants are to be done, I want more on the Baal-Hadaad.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we have the War of the Pure and even a good amount of Skinchangers focused on the Shadow. Again, as far as my own interests goes, that's a cue to me to say &quot;Time to break the mold.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as we translate the existing stuff into the new edition while we're at it, I'll be down for new and shiny things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:31:16-08:00","id":840885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840880#post840880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we do get more Helios-servants, I really hope they're some variety of werereptiles. I mean, it works thematically, since reptiles=sun. Although, honestly, I mostly just want it because I LOVE reptiles. Maybe even make them more technologically/civilization-focused than Werewolves? It makes for a good dichotomy, and there's a lot of mythological association between reptiles and knowledge/cunning/so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are already plenty attached to technology and civilization: none of the Forsaken tribes are particularly anti-civilization or technology, and plenty of packs have territories in cities.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with attaching werereptiles to the Sun, but I don't think werewolves are sufficiently anti-technology or pro-rural to set up Helion weres as their technologically-biased opposites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:09:23-08:00","id":840911,"title":"","content":"Thinking on topic to not recreate mistakes of 1ED Changing Breeds - <b>first and foremost -</b> <b>Quality over Quantity</b>. In previous reincarnation we had like 100 Breeds with text a bit more like 2ED <b>Changling</b>'s Kiths. It was too much, to different and not playtested mechanically. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>I would much rather see 20 cool, detailed and retested Breeds with chapter &quot;How to make your Breed&quot; and many Dread Powers for them, than see another 100 half-backed.</b> With about 20 we could have two examples with all 10 Breeds - that's enough to have some general cool ideas, some proper mechanics and left space for fans to write more. Much better to give us tools to create themselves new Breeds as we love to do it and better to have few but strong examples in book.<br /> <br /> Also, I can totally see other Beast-Blooded as Lesser Template for &quot;werecurse afflicted&quot;, like with Uratha and their lesser kin - various Beast-Blooded would easily eat ( or even become ) various Skinchangers. Once again, much more like to see toolbox here to create my own.<br /> <br /> <b>As to Shadow relations with &quot;ferals&quot; - I think that large Optional Rules would be enough - think about here like <i>Fathers Form</i> essay in Werewolf 2ED.</b> Myself, I would pick only particular Breeds to be connected to Shadow, rest of them to be general &quot;Chronicles of Darkness weirdness&quot;, not having anything to gods and totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:17:08-08:00","id":840915,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think a 2e Changing Breeds needs to have a from-the-ground-up approach taken, including a very long, hard look taken at what the actual purpose of the book would be in the context of the ChroD setting and as a tool for games. It's a great opportunity to look at the horror around metamorphosis and body horror, and I think a new version that was just a roster of breeds and special rules thereof would be a waste of a chance to make it something other than the book that lets people play weredeer or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:22:03-08:00","id":840918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840915#post840915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think a 2e Changing Breeds needs to have a from-the-ground-up approach taken, including a very long, hard look taken at what the actual purpose of the book would be in the context of the ChroD setting and as a tool for games. It's a great opportunity to look at the horror around metamorphosis and body horror, and I think a new version that was just a roster of breeds and special rules thereof would be a waste of a chance to make it something other than the book that lets people play weredeer or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we need to get folkies together and chat about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T14:27:21-08:00","id":840920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840918#post840918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why we need to get folkies together and chat about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have my sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/