"user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T15:16:52-08:00","id":840942,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question, is Skinchangers considered more of a Werewolf supplement or a Blue Book one? So if I had a skinchanger idea, where would I post it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T15:33:17-08:00","id":840950,"title":"","content":"Blue book, so general area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:02:44-08:00","id":840963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840920#post840920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have my sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>And my axe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:17:42-08:00","id":840974,"title":"","content":"Well that's great guys, but what I need is coffee and money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:38:46-08:00","id":840998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840974#post840974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's great guys, but what I need is coffee and money.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We'd need a kickstarter to get you the money.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the coffee, well, I guess some of us can mail you junk right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:31:43-08:00","id":841050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840911#post840911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As to Shadow relations with &quot;ferals&quot; - I think that large Optional Rules would be enough - think about here like <i>Fathers Form</i> essay in Werewolf 2ED.</b> Myself, I would pick only particular Breeds to be connected to Shadow, rest of them to be general &quot;Chronicles of Darkness weirdness&quot;, not having anything to gods and totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally, the book would have both and then some. Room to explore weird body horror, one-off Claimed variants that act more like full skin-changers, as well as those who tread between worlds. Each chapter could easily focus on a specific kind of thing. Have the first chapter be the rules, maybe, with a vast toolkit for constructing various skin-changers, beast-blooded, and werebeasts. The following chapters could be explorations of various kinds of shapeshifter stories, with plenty of sample werecreatures statted up (some one-off deals, some &quot;Breeds&quot;), and fluff to go with them. You could have the cursed kind, the born kind, and the stolen kind, with plenty of plot hooks and advice for using them in chronicles.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:00:35-08:00","id":841060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840915#post840915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think a 2e Changing Breeds needs to have a from-the-ground-up approach taken, including a very long, hard look taken at what the actual purpose of the book would be in the context of the ChroD setting and as a tool for games. It's a great opportunity to look at the horror around metamorphosis and body horror, and I think a new version that was just a roster of breeds and special rules thereof would be a waste of a chance to make it something other than the book that lets people play weredeer or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having just completed my 1e to 2e hacks of the Changing Breeds book, I could not agree more.<br /> <br /> Also, huge +1 for Claire's rough outline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:05:19-08:00","id":841075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840477#post840477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be the first to jump at such a project. Seriously, it's on my character sheet and everything! &quot;<b>Changing Breeds: </b>Claire gains an infinite bonus to her Initiative when acting to be part of any new Changing Breeds book.&quot; The Fera were my favorite things in the oWoD and also include my favorite playable species in a game (the Mokol\u00e9), and I would enjoy having the opportunity to bring more werebeasts and skin-changers into the Chronicles. Note that, like every book is assumed to be, this is part of a toolkit experience, so you wouldn't have to include all or even any of them in your games. No werezoo unless you want to include everything, but for those who do want some variety, you can have your werecrocodiles and weresharks and wereparaceratheriums. The last one might be a joke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Maybe.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Lets hope you get it, Claire! I think there is a lot of potential in another shifters, since the Forsaken are never going to run out of things to Hunt, or to compete against for whatever it is the other shifters want. Be it sons and daughters from other spirit creatures to something wholy different, I think it would only benefit the Forsaken template to have more to their world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:10:33-08:00","id":841106,"title":"","content":"The Bull ones make sense since they're connected with Helios, but do the others have connections?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T22:23:09-08:00","id":841139,"title":"","content":"If I can proposed something in Toolkit chapter - <b>Banes of each &quot;Breed&quot; can be taken from long list.</b> Uratha have Silver, some others could have Gold, Bronze or other &quot;Sacred Metal&quot; on same principle - but <i>others</i> should have truly bizzare Banes. Like wood, children bones, etc. It all can be connected to new &quot;Primal Urge&quot; mechanics stating that Bane is making PU damage, and like.<br /> <br /> I think this would highted the horror / wierdness aspect, but also could make easier change to the Bane in examples if ST and gaming group did not like those in book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T23:01:41-08:00","id":841150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841060#post841060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having just completed my 1e to 2e hacks of the Changing Breeds book, I could not agree more.<br /> <br /> Also, huge +1 for Claire's rough outline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where is that? I'm interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T00:52:57-08:00","id":841177,"title":"","content":"One of most crucial question about Changing Breeds 2ED is this - <b>Does it should be general Chronicles of Darkness or Werewolf specific supplement?</b> I mean here questions like could we use mirror Major Templates with names like Harmony, Primal Urge, Forms and a like? And even if we use those - will they be the same thing? I would more lean in to general CoD supplement, especially as Devs are marking that they want to make more horror/weird shapchangers. <br /> <br /> Harmony is major nut to crack here - for Uratha, balance for Flesh and Spirit is logical, as they are beings of two worlds. However, if Breeds are more open to &quot;non-Shadow&quot; relation, their Harmony could mean different things. Balance between human and animal. Balannce between human and environment ( if devs will go this rote ). Or even &quot;Integrity to override Rage&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>And we go to the concepts like Rage there - Is it need to be in new Breeds?</b> It's interesting to see them in Uratha, but what about fox-changers? What was take on this matter in <b>War Againt The Pure</b>?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T05:57:53-08:00","id":841246,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd prefer something more Werewolf specific. &quot;Breeds&quot; that don't use Harmony can use Integrity (or nothing at all, just like Horrors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:46:08-08:00","id":841271,"title":"","content":"Except you'd want them immune to lunacy, and swapping out their integrity for an equivalent is the easiest way of doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T13:41:28-08:00","id":841480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841139#post841139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can proposed something in Toolkit chapter - <b>Banes of each &quot;Breed&quot; can be taken from long list.</b> Uratha have Silver, some others could have Gold, Bronze or other &quot;Sacred Metal&quot; on same principle - but <i>others</i> should have truly bizzare Banes. Like wood, children bones, etc. It all can be connected to new &quot;Primal Urge&quot; mechanics stating that Bane is making PU damage, and like.<br /> <br /> I think this would highted the horror / wierdness aspect, but also could make easier change to the Bane in examples if ST and gaming group did not like those in book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be you simply have to view the &quot;Breeds as symbolism&quot; to end up at a logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Personally would like to have a Theme for each breed rather than simply there for the sake of being there. Grouping by ideological niche and corresponding ecological niche (Herds, predators, scavengers, parasites, etc) and a method of gaining essence in terms of acting out that niche is a nice carrot for players and a in-game universe reason of why Bird Man fights so hard in the court room (the predator mindset helps) and Ms Roach works in the scrap yard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841050#post841050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideally, the book would have both and then some. Room to explore weird body horror, one-off Claimed variants that act more like full skin-changers, as well as those who tread between worlds. Each chapter could easily focus on a specific kind of thing. Have the first chapter be the rules, maybe, with a vast toolkit for constructing various skin-changers, beast-blooded, and werebeasts. The following chapters could be explorations of various kinds of shapeshifter stories, with plenty of sample werecreatures statted up (some one-off deals, some &quot;Breeds&quot;), and fluff to go with them. You could have the cursed kind, the born kind, and the stolen kind, with plenty of plot hooks and advice for using them in chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always had my eye on the cursed and stolen kind. That social horror aspect has been the domain of Vampire (with Changeling thrown in) but can work especially well here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 03-03-2016, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T23:44:28-08:00","id":841752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841480#post841480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to be you simply have to view the &quot;Breeds as symbolism&quot; to end up at a logical endpoint.<br /> <br /> Personally would like to have a Theme for each breed rather than simply there for the sake of being there. Grouping by ideological niche and corresponding ecological niche (Herds, predators, scavengers, parasites, etc) and a method of gaining essence in terms of acting out that niche is a nice carrot for players and a in-game universe reason of why Bird Man fights so hard in the court room (the predator mindset helps) and Ms Roach works in the scrap yard.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want to end the Breeds devisions on Cats, Bears, Lizards, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T09:27:31-08:00","id":841938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841752#post841752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you want to end the Breeds devisions on Cats, Bears, Lizards, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a step above that. Grouping breeds on what they do would help out. Cats are predators, same with birds of prey, sharks and the like. The benefit is that it would help with any existential crisis that a ST would have in adding them to game with the drawback being that it would snip some of the creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T10:42:30-08:00","id":841984,"title":"","content":"But &quot;what they do&quot; was idea of Accords - and I very liked Accords. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That you could play werecat as predator, loving mother or genius cat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-04-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:37:59-08:00","id":842029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841984#post841984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But &quot;what they do&quot; was idea of Accords - and I very liked Accords.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That you could play were cat as predator, loving mother or genius cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer accords to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless shock means about a different &quot;What they do&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:41:11-08:00","id":842031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841984#post841984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But &quot;what they do&quot; was idea of Accords - and I very liked Accords.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That you could play were cat as predator, loving mother or genius cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Screw predator bunnies, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:36:01-08:00","id":842079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=842031#post842031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Screw predator bunnies, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. <br /> <br /> I hate to break it to you but herbivores are frequently more dangerous to humans than predators. More people get killed each year by mooses, elks, and bison than by bears, wolves, or great cats. Violence is a function of size.<br /> <br /> Also bunnies are cannibals...just throwing that out there.<br /> <br /> (For the record though, I always thought that the Accords were terrible, so much so I jettisoned them for my update hacks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:59:35-08:00","id":842103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841984#post841984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But &quot;what they do&quot; was idea of Accords - and I very liked Accords.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That you could play were cat as predator, loving mother or genius cat.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>The Wolf Must Hunt</b></i><br /> <br /> Nothing is stopping a character from playing those concepts but the Accords were, to put simply, not really useful in either play or in helping the ST think of a reason of how to fit them into sessions.<br /> <br /> Seems to me that grouping them by ecological roles first and then giving a single simple line (<b><i>Wolf Must hunt</i></b>, <b><i>Shark Must Swim</i></b>, etc) on that specific breed would help farther define it's purpose and theme. Can characters buck against the trend and theme of the Breed? Sure. The Uratha can try to be pacifists. The deck in terms of instincts and ability (not to mention attention from the Shadow) has it stack against them but sure. They are human after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:27:04-08:00","id":842578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=842079#post842079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh.<br /> <br /> I hate to break it to you but herbivores are frequently more dangerous to humans than predators. More people get killed each year by mooses, elks, and bison than by bears, wolves, or great cats. Violence is a function of size.<br /> <br /> Also bunnies are cannibals...just throwing that out there.<br /> <br /> (For the record though, I always thought that the Accords were terrible, so much so I jettisoned them for my update hacks.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Doh. Not because of predation. Sure. Herbivores can often one-up their predators. Otherwise, they would have gotten extinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:53:44-08:00","id":842785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=842578#post842578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doh. Not because of predation. Sure. Herbivores can often one-up their predators. Otherwise, they would have gotten extinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, in the end, I feel like shifter potential has less to do with the actual scientific/biological realities of the animal and more with the cultural resonance it has. And there are plenty of herbivores that have interesting cultural niches that could be explored. We already have minotaurs in WtF, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T17:54:08-08:00","id":842811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=842785#post842785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in the end, I feel like shifter potential has less to do with the actual scientific/biological realities of the animal and more with the cultural resonance it has. And there are plenty of herbivores that have interesting cultural niches that could be explored. We already have minotaurs in WtF, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you imagine these assholes in India?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T05:25:15-08:00","id":842953,"title":"","content":"On the note of cultural resonance, I'd like to post a link to some of my favorite homebrew material on the Forums:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8823-new-shifters-the-water-horses\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8823-new-shifters-the-water-horses\"> New Shifters: The Water Horses - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8823-new-shifters-the-water-horses\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8823-new-shifters-the-water-horses </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> [Material from the old forums] Same as the others, they have their own parallel-wolf mechanical build, but it wouldn't be difficult to transform them into standard WatP shapeshifters -- keep the relevant forms, give them shapeshifting and regeneration, and figure the Clan boons to be their third main power. </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd also like to point them out as an example of how to connect Shapeshifters to a realm other than the Shadow (in this case - the Underworld).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T06:56:38-08:00","id":842965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840622#post840622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do mountains symbolize? Permanence, immovability, fortitde, obstacles on paths to greater things or danger. From there you have long-lived and hearty beings that challenge others to better themselves or treacherously to doom them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There a fuckton of mythological and literary mentors or tutelary guardians that could describe.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, you have something like John Hawksmoor from the Authority. A Man of Cities. Were-emotions would resemble some of the thousands of examples we've had of rageful beings throughout history. Something demonic, red-skinned, heated and steaming or smoking. </div> </div> </div>Were-emotions might turn into something akin to the Whisperers from Inferno - sort of like how the Wendigo (a spirit of hunger and desperation, from one perspective) could variously be a physical monster, a possessing spirit, a transformed human, or a mental condition. Were-territory might be a bizarre explanation for interstitial terrain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=840660#post840660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a while I've felt that the essential problem* of Changing Breeds was trying to be cWoD in nWoD, and it just didn't fit or work at all as that. But I like the concept of additional shifters in the CofD/nWoD, and it has a lot of material worth exploring. The shifters in WATP for instance, were quite unique and very thematically different from the Uratha. They're a good example of what I'd want to see in a Forsaken 2e supplement about other shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the points Ethan Skemp has occasionally made about Werewolf the Forsaken is that werewolves weren't &quot;meant to be&quot; - they're an accidental phenomenon that happened to become successful - in that light, WAtP avoided a trap of fitting its shapeshifters into a spectrum of purposes the way the OWoD's were - some might believe they have a purpose, but it won't meaningfully relate to the Uratha's except by accident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839512-other-shapeshifters-and-skinchangers-in-2e?p=841177#post841177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of most crucial question about Changing Breeds 2ED is this - <b>Does it should be general Chronicles of Darkness or Werewolf specific supplement?</b> I mean here questions like could we use mirror Major Templates with names like Harmony, Primal Urge, Forms and a like? And even if we use those - will they be the same thing? I would more lean in to general CoD supplement, especially as Devs are marking that they want to make more horror/weird shapchangers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harmony is major nut to crack here - for Uratha, balance for Flesh and Spirit is logical, as they are beings of two worlds. However, if Breeds are more open to &quot;non-Shadow&quot; relation, their Harmony could mean different things. Balance between human and animal. Balannce between human and environment ( if devs will go this rote ). Or even &quot;Integrity to override Rage&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I could see a different Integritype for each broad type of origin. If you're a Hisil hybrid of some sort, then a Harmony like that of werewolves makes sense. If you're a human twisted by weird magical forces, then keeping Integrity (or something like Vampire's Humanity) sounds like the ticket. Beings that draw from the Astral might have something more like Synergy - not a tension between two beings, but between a driving inner nature and human self, with benefits deriving from how closely they accord. Synergy <i>might</i> be a model for a general Integritype, since &quot;driving inner nature&quot; is something we can expect all of these shapeshifters to have.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}